spans.s:
úpa,
 —1. vbl prefix. to, unto, toward; opp.
of ápa;
 —2. prep., w. acc., unto, 81^15;
w. loc., in, 77^5;
 —3. in noun cpds [1289b],
denoting something near, accessory, or subordinate.
[cf. ὑπο, Lat. s-ub, ‘under.’]

upacārá, m. a coming to or waiting upon;
 pregnantly, (polite) attention; (correct)
procedure, i. e. duty. [√car + upa.]

upamá-śravas, a. having highest glory;
as m. Upamaśravas, a name like Μεγιστο-
κλῆς or Ὑψι-κλῆς.

upāntá, n. proximity to the end; edge;
immediate neighborhood. [upa (mg 3) +
anta.]
